    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d637">

                <pb facs="0763" n="643" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg643"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to Ambassador
                        Clayton.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-03-21"><hi rendition="#italic">March 21,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1256.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your telegram of the 16th
                    instant concerning the fears of the Yaqui Copper Company of depredations by
                    Yaqui Indians at Santo Niño, Sonora, I inclose herewith for your information a
                    copy of the company’s letter of the 15th instant,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d637-f1"
                    /> giving further information in the matter and alleging that the authorities of
                    the State of Sonora do not exert themselves as they ought toward protecting the
                    lives and property of American citizens engaged in mining in that state.</p>
                <p>The Department would be pleased to have a report from you of the facts of the
                    case.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Alvey A. Adee.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
